menu "Hawk communicator emulator"

config HAWK_WIFI_LOG
    bool "WiFi UDP live-log broadcast (debug only; needs main/wifi_creds.h)"
    default n
    help
        Mirror every ESP_LOG line as a UDP broadcast on port 5556 so a PC on the
        LAN can watch the communicator while it is plugged into a distant Xbox
        controller. When enabled, main/wifi_log.c is compiled and requires a
        local, gitignored main/wifi_creds.h with your SSID/password (copy
        main/wifi_creds.h.example).

        Keep this OFF for real Xbox tests until proven harmless for this device:
        on Falcon (same board, heavier iso traffic), joining WiFi loaded the
        CPU/radio enough to break the Xbox's timing-strict USB enumeration. It
        is off by default so the project builds with no secrets present.

endmenu
